                <pb facs="0787" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11526: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-08T16:00:00+08:00">December 8, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 8—9:41 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. A representative of a foreign Embassy stated this morning that a few days ago
                    42 Soviet planes arrived in Nanchang bringing about 100 Soviet flyers and other
                    aviation personnel, also that about 50 Soviet flyers are in Hankow and a number
                    of planes including an efficient pursuit plane. This information has not been
                    confirmed but is regarded as probably reliable.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai, Nanking, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
